            <div xml:id="d1144">

                <pb facs="1164" n="1154" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg1154"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.115/10–2449: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">McConaughy</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-10-24T13:00:00+08:00">October 24, 1949—1
                            p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 24—2:46 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4491. A. P. Pattison, Shanghai agent Isbrandtsen Company, informs Consulate
                    General [that] SS <hi rendition="#italic">Flying Cloud</hi> ETD Hong Kong
                    October 24 or 25 for Shanghai. Cargo for Shanghai discharged about 6,000
                    tons.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 4491, repeated Hong Kong 334.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">McConaughy</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
